The macOS options of the bcm2837 machine. macOS userspace and the macOS kexts need the
parts of Apple's MASTER.arm64.MacOSX that the iPhoneOS-based machine file leaves out: System V
IPC, sendfile, disk quotas (the HFS quota KPIs), /.vol paths, setuid on mounts, the external
resolver, searchfs, firmlinks and file leases, mount by role (Data, VM, Preboot and Recovery), AppleDouble files, nullfs, the commpage preemption-free zone that macOS
libplatform calls for OSAtomicFifo, audit, CSR with its configuration from the device tree,
supplemental signatures and a second static trust cache. The rest of the machine file, the
memory and code signing configuration proven on this board, stays as it is. Only the macOS
profile applies this patch; iPadOS reads the machine file unchanged.
